IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `epd-nouns`
IMPORT `epd-seat`
IMPORT `epd-seat-sender`

-- MIRROR CASES. The same message and the same facts, put to the recipient's seat (the individual) and to the sender's seat.
-- Each scenario below is two assertions of the same expected value (written from the text, not from the output) and a third
-- that the two seats' answers are equal. Both seats call the same layer-1 function, so they cannot disagree about the law;
-- these cases show it, and show that each seat's inputs carry the same facts.

-- I42 (the recipient) against S1 (the sender): Art 13 the message may be sent to the recipient
-- Mirror 1: a marketing e-mail the recipient consented to beforehand.
#ASSERT (`May this marketing message be sent to me` WITH `the message reached me by` IS `an electronic mail message`, `the message is for direct marketing` IS TRUE, `I did not ask for the message` IS TRUE, `I am a natural person` IS TRUE, `I gave my consent beforehand` IS TRUE, `the sender got my details from me as its customer` IS FALSE, `I gave them when buying a product or service` IS TRUE, `I gave them lawfully under Directive 95/46/EC` IS TRUE, `the sender is the business I bought from` IS TRUE, `the message sells the sender's own products or services` IS TRUE, `the products or services are similar to what I bought` IS TRUE, `I was clearly and distinctly offered a way to object` IS TRUE, `the offer to object was free` IS TRUE, `the offer to object was easy` IS TRUE, `I was offered it when the details were collected` IS TRUE, `I refused at the start` IS FALSE, `I was offered it with every message` IS TRUE, `the sender's identity is disguised or concealed` IS FALSE, `the message breaks Article 6 of Directive 2000/31/EC` IS FALSE, `there is no valid address to ask them to stop` IS FALSE, `the message pushes me to a website that breaks that Article` IS FALSE, `national law has chosen` IS `national legislation has not been stated`, `I do not wish to receive these messages` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`May I send this marketing message to this recipient` WITH `how I send it` IS `an electronic mail message`, `my message is for direct marketing` IS TRUE, `the recipient did not ask for it` IS TRUE, `the recipient is a natural person` IS TRUE, `the recipient consented beforehand` IS TRUE, `I got the recipient's details from the recipient as my customer` IS FALSE, `I got them in the context of a sale` IS TRUE, `I got them in accordance with Directive 95/46/EC` IS TRUE, `I am the same person that got the details` IS TRUE, `I am marketing my own products or services` IS TRUE, `they are similar to what the recipient bought` IS TRUE, `I clearly and distinctly offered the recipient a way to object` IS TRUE, `the offer to object was free` IS TRUE, `the offer to object was easy` IS TRUE, `I offered it when I collected the details` IS TRUE, `the recipient initially refused such use` IS FALSE, `I offered it with each message` IS TRUE, `my message disguises or conceals who I am` IS FALSE, `my message breaks Article 6 of Directive 2000/31/EC` IS FALSE, `my message has no valid address for requests to stop` IS FALSE, `my message pushes the recipient to a website that breaks that Article` IS FALSE, `national law has chosen` IS `national legislation has not been stated`, `the recipient does not wish to receive these messages` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
